AN7581: static-HIR record selection with self-evidence readbacks (010).

Design: devices/ZN504XG-D/reports/patch010_design_20261030.md (user-approved
2026-10-30 22:43).  This patch REPLACES 009: the runtime HIR read
(readl(0x1faf0064)) that 009 introduced hangs the old unit's SoC bus in
kernel mode mid-boot - the build-18 boot loop, evidenced by serial log
(the "HIR %x" print never appears before the watchdog reset; H-24).
The OEM-order bring-up itself is unchanged; only the record selection
becomes static by default and the dangerous read becomes opt-in.

Changes (en75xx_zsi.c, non-legacy path, plus en75xx_slic_le9642.c):

  - hir_read default flips 1 -> 0 and the parameter description now
    carries the old-unit hazard; hir_read=1 keeps the OEM runtime GET_HIR
    read for the NEW unit only.
  - New parameter hir_record (uint, default 0xe): static record group
    0xa/0xc/0xe = record 2/3/4, 0 = no chipScuReg record.  Used whenever
    hir_read=0, so the old unit applies the live-machine signature
    record without touching the poison window.
  - New parameter clkscu_rb (default 1): after the OEM record RMW the
    driver reads both clocksrc registers back and prints them - the P1
    acceptance evidence lands in dmesg, no devmem needed (0x1fa2xxxx
    is a safe read region).
  - New parameter slic_probe_dump (default 1) in the slic driver: after
    the VP-API init path completes it reads SWCTRL(0xe7)/DEVMODE/
    CLKSLOTS/TXSLOT/RXSLOT and prints them - the P2 acceptance evidence
    (OEM targets DEVMODE=14 00 / CLKSLOTS=46 / TX=03 / RX=04).
  - Probe banner now also reports hir_record and clkscu_rb.
  - reset_oem_bits / zsi2_en_auto / cfg_write / clocksrc_arg1 carry over
    from 009 unchanged (defaults 1/1/0/0).

Defaults make the old unit boot unmodified; every A/B axis is a runtime
module parameter, so one build runs the whole verification matrix.

Risks: hir_read=1 on the old unit reproduces the build-18 boot loop by
design - never set it there.  reset_oem_bits=1 (SYS_RESET bit17/25 OEM
pulses) is still untested on the old unit (build-18 died earlier at the
HIR read); if P0 fails, A/B it first with reset_oem_bits=0.

Acceptance (build-19, layered gate, serial console mandatory):
  P0: dmesg shows "ZSI transport ready ( ... hir_read 0, hir_record e ...)"
      then "Le964%c detected (rcn 08 pcn 49)" instead of "unexpected chip
      id ff ff".  Sentinel: the literal "HIR " banner must NOT appear.
  P1: "clkscu readback" line matches the live-machine table families
      (0x1fa20214/0x1fa20218 and 0x1fa201d0/0x1fa201cc).
  P2: "SLIC probe dump" line shows SWCTRL != 0 and the OEM target values,
      then dial tone on the FXS port.

Signed-off-by: ZN504XG-D voice porting project
